              "category": "method_choice",
              "title": "No justification for Fisher's exact test over chi-square with n=240",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "stats-run/stats-run.json: method 'fisher-exact'"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Standard approach for 2x2 tables with expected counts >5 is chi-square; Fisher's is typically for small samples or sparse tables. Method choice should be explained.",
              "actionableFix": "Justify the choice, e.g., if any expected cell count <5, or if exact test preferred for robustness. Provide expected counts.",
